<title>UK: Burmah up as SocGen repeats &quot;buy&quot; stance.</title>
<headline>Burmah up as SocGen repeats &quot;buy&quot; stance.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Burmah Castrol Plc rose 30-1/2p to 10.66-1/2 stg by 0930 GMT in a generally weaker oil sector on Thursday as broker SocGen reiterated its &quot;buy&quot; recommendation for the oil company.</p>
<p>&quot;We have always liked Burmah. We still see it as a buy,&quot; a spokesman at SocGen said.</p>
<p>&quot;At the moment many are bullish on Burmah&quot;, he said, adding that a lack of liquidity could give the share a further boost.</p>
<p>On Wednesday analysts at brokerage Kleinwort Benson rated Burmah a buy, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
